IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sfa-core`
IMPORT `sfa-periods`
IMPORT `sfad-debentures`

-- Securities and Futures Act 2001 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation (a rendering, not the official text).
-- Layer 1, part sfad: the answers sfad gives to the questions sfac asks of it (seams S4 and S5 of inputs/PLAN.md section 4.1; seam S3 is answered
-- by `s 280(1) the offer is an offer referred to in section 280` in sfad-ois-intl-gov-atm.l4).
-- Imports prelude, daydate, sfa-core, sfa-periods and sfad-debentures (for section 262(3)).
--
-- How to read a function in this module: each answers a question of sfac's as a BOOLEAN, because PLAN.md fixes the type of the seam input as BOOLEAN.
--   A BOOLEAN has no third value: where the sections' own functions answer NOTHING (not known, or not covered), the seam answer is FALSE, which here means "not shown to hold".
--   "-- FORK" lines are collected into the fork register of NOTES.md.

§ `Subdivision (4): the offer qualifies for an exemption (seam S4)`

DECLARE `Subdivision (4) an exemption relied on` HAS
    `the provision of the exemption` IS A STRING
    `the answer of the provision` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `the exemption has been revoked under section 281` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the exemptions` IS A LIST OF `Subdivision (4) an exemption relied on`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Subdivision (4) the number of exemptions that hold and have not been revoked` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the exemptions`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN 0
    WHEN e FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        IF ((e's `the answer of the provision`) EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (NOT (e's `the exemption has been revoked under section 281`))
        THEN 1 PLUS (`Subdivision (4) the number of exemptions that hold and have not been revoked` rest)
        ELSE `Subdivision (4) the number of exemptions that hold and have not been revoked` rest

-- src:42644 | Subdivision (4) — Exemptions
@ref Subdivision (4) (src:42644-42644)
GIVEN
    `the exemptions` IS A LIST OF `Subdivision (4) an exemption relied on` @desc For each exemption of Subdivision (4) of Division 1 of Part 13 (other than section 280) that the offer might come within (sections 272(1), 272(2), 272A(1), 272B(1), 273(1), 273(5) with the date of the declaration, 274, 275(1), 275(1A), 277(1), 277(1AC), 278(1) and 279): the provision's label, what its function answers (NOTHING if you do not know), and whether the exemption has been revoked under section 281.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Subdivision (4) the offer qualifies for an exemption under Subdivision (4) of Division 1 of Part 13, other than section 280` MEANS
    (`Subdivision (4) the number of exemptions that hold and have not been revoked` `the exemptions`) AT LEAST 1
    -- FORK sum-S4 | Subdivision (4) | `Subdivision (4) the offer qualifies for an exemption under Subdivision (4) of Division 1 of Part 13, other than section 280` | took the offer as qualifying when at least one exemption of the Subdivision (other than section 280) is shown to hold (its function answers JUST TRUE) and has not been revoked under section 281; FALSE where none is shown, including where an answer is NOTHING (PLAN.md section 4.1 types the seam input as BOOLEAN, so the third value cannot cross it) | other reading a revoked exemption still "qualifies" until the review of section 281(2) ends; or a three-valued seam in which NOTHING stays NOTHING | licence the seam's type in PLAN.md and the text of section 281(1) ("revoke any exemption under this Subdivision"), which makes a revoked exemption no longer an exemption the offer can rely on. Section 280 is left out, as the question names it ("other than section 280").

§ `s 262(3): asset-backed securities (seam S5)`

-- src:41894 | “asset‑backed securities” means debentures or units of
-- src:41895 | debentures issued pursuant to a securitisation transaction;
@ref s 262(3) (src:41894-41895)
GIVEN
    `the securities are debentures or units of debentures` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the securities debentures or units of debentures?
    `the securities are issued pursuant to a securitisation transaction` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for section 262(3) "securitisation transaction" answer for the arrangement the securities are issued under? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 262(3) the securities are asset-backed securities as section 262(3) defines them` MEANS
    (`s 262(3) the securities are asset-backed securities` `the securities are debentures or units of debentures` `the securities are issued pursuant to a securitisation transaction`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
    -- FORK sum-S5 | s 262(3) | `s 262(3) the securities are asset-backed securities as section 262(3) defines them` | took the securities as asset-backed securities only where section 262(3)'s own function answers JUST TRUE; FALSE where it answers JUST FALSE or NOTHING (PLAN.md section 4.1 types the seam input as BOOLEAN) | other reading a three-valued seam in which NOTHING stays NOTHING | licence the seam's type in PLAN.md
